# SP+ SOFTWARE MANIFEST — what an advisor's machine must actually contain.
# Source of truth: projects/sp-plus/Containerfile (the intended product).
# Format: TYPE|NAME|WHY
# TYPE: rpm | path | unit | user
rpm|plasma-workspace|the desktop itself
rpm|sddm|graphical login — without it there is no login screen
rpm|cups|printing, the single most common advisor support call
rpm|cups-filters|printing
rpm|cups-pk-helper|lets a non-root advisor add a printer
rpm|firewalld|host firewall, a compliance talking point
rpm|NetworkManager-wifi|wifi on a laptop
rpm|bluez|bluetooth
rpm|blueman|bluetooth GUI an advisor can actually use
rpm|pipewire|audio, for client video calls
rpm|wireplumber|audio session manager
rpm|xdg-desktop-portal-kde|file pickers and screen share in Plasma
rpm|udisks2|USB media handling
rpm|python3|the SP+ runtime is written in it
rpm|curl|runtime dependency
rpm|ca-certificates|TLS trust
rpm|jq|runtime dependency
rpm|sudo|advisor is in wheel
rpm|brave-browser|THE advisor-facing application
path|/usr/libexec/sp-plus/spplus_rpc.py|the SP+ RPC runtime
path|/usr/libexec/sp-plus/pwa|the advisor PWA
path|/usr/libexec/sp-plus/knowledge|knowledge base
path|/usr/libexec/sp-plus/playbooks|remediation playbooks
path|/usr/libexec/sp-plus/playbooks/printer-reconnect.json.sha256|playbook integrity stamp
path|/etc/brave/policies/managed/sp-plus.json|managed Brave policy
unit|sp-plus.service|the SP+ service
unit|sddm.service|graphical login
unit|cups.service|printing
unit|firewalld.service|firewall
user|advisor|the advisor account must exist
